Steven Scheirer, Noah Wisdom and Valentina Zapata Castro, “On minimal bases in homotopical combinatorics”, arXiv:2506.11159 (2025).\n\nThe simple-and-double-rainbow conjecture for $C_{p^nq^m}$C p n q m​\n\nConjecture openOpen about 1 year · documented by 2025\n\nLet $p$p and $q$q be distinct primes and let $n\\geqslant m\\geqslant2$n⩾m⩾2. Write $\\mathfrak{c}(C_{p^nq^m})$c(C p n q m​) for the complexity of $C_{p^nq^m}$C p n q m​. A simple rainbow and a double rainbow are the constructions defined in the paper, and the paper also defines the set obtained from a double rainbow in the cited construction. Simple-and-double-rainbow conjecture. The complexity of $C_{p^nq^m}$C p n q m​ is realized by a simple rainbow, unless $n+m$n+m is even and $m=2$m=2; in that exceptional case, it is realized by the set obtained from a double rainbow. This conjecture is based on computer calculations and tabulated values, and gives a uniform description of which rainbow construction realizes the complexity.\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\nsource: Katharine Adamyk, Scott Balchin, Miguel Barrero, Steven Scheirer, Noah Wisdom and Valentina Zapata Castro, “On minimal bases in homotopical combinatorics”, arXiv:2506.11159 (2025).\n\ngroup-theoryhomotopical-combinatorics\n\n0\n\nposted by arXiv 3 days ago\n\n\n## 0 Replies\n\n* * *\n\nSign in to reply.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConjecture on polygonal extremals in the convex (lambda_1,mu_1)-diagram | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/366508/conjecture-on-polygonal-extremals-in-the-convex-lambda-1-mu)\nciteturn5search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; # Conjecture on polygonal extremals in the convex $(\\lambda_1,\\mu_1)$(λ 1​,μ 1​)-diagram ... Ilias Ftouhi and Antoine Henrot, “The diagram (λ_1,μ_1)”, arXiv:2501.02283 (2025).\n\n# Conjecture on polygonal extremals in the convex $(\\lambda_1,\\mu_1)$(λ 1​,μ 1​)-diagram\n\n1 year old · traced to 2025\n\nLet $\\mathcal{E}^C$E C be the $(\\lambda_1,\\mu_1)$(λ 1​,μ 1​)-diagram for planar convex domains, with domains normalized to have area $1$1. Let $B$B be a ball, let $T_e$T e​ be the equilateral triangle of unit area, and write $\\lambda_1(\\Omega)$λ 1​(Ω) and $\\mu_1(\\Omega)$μ 1​(Ω) for the first Dirichlet and Neumann eigenvalues. For a fixed $\\ell$ℓ, consider maximizers of $\\mu_1(\\Omega)$μ 1​(Ω) among convex domains satisfying $\\lambda_1(\\Omega)=\\ell$λ 1​(Ω)=ℓ and $|\\Omega|=1$∣Ω∣=1.\n\nConjecture on polygonal extremals. Except for the ball, domains on the upper boundary of $\\mathcal{E}^C$E C are polygonal; regular polygons lie on that upper boundary; and there exists $x_0>\\lambda_1(T_e)$x 0​>λ 1​(T e​) such that: if $\\ell\\in[\\lambda_1(T_e),x_0)$ℓ∈[λ 1​(T e​),x 0​), a maximizer is a superequilateral triangle; if $\\ell\\in(x_0,+\\infty)$ℓ∈(x 0​,+∞), a maximizer is a rectangle; and at $\\ell=x_0$ℓ=x 0​, both a rectangle and a superequilateral triangle solve the maximization problem.\n\nThese claims are based on numerical experiments with random convex polygons. They propose a detailed description of the upper boundary and its extremal domains, but no proof or resolution is supplied in the text.\n\nReferences\n\n  1. Ilias Ftouhi and Antoine Henrot, “The diagram (λ_1,μ_1)”, arXiv:2501.02283 (2025).\n\nconvex-geometryshape-optimizationspectral-geometry--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe diagram $(\\lambda_1,\\mu_1)$ — Scifaro (https://scifaro.com/en/abs/the-diagram-lambda-1-mu-1-2501.02283)\nciteturn5search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago;     @article{arxiv.2501.02283,\n\nHome › Optimization and Control › The diagram $(\\lambda_1,\\mu_1)$\n\n# The diagram $(\\lambda_1,\\mu_1)$\n\nOptimization and Control 2025-01-07 v1\n\nAuthors: Ilias Ftouhi , Antoine Henrot\n\nView on arXiv ↗ PDF ↗\n\n### Abstract\n\nIn this paper, we are interested in the possible values taken by the pair $(\\lambda_1(\\Omega), \\mu_1(\\Omega))$(λ 1​(Ω),μ 1​(Ω)) the first eigenvalues of the Laplace operator with Dirichlet and Neumann boundary conditions respectively of a bounded plane domain $\\Omega$Ω. We prove that, without any particular assumption on the class of open sets $\\Omega$Ω, the two classical inequalities (the Faber-Krahn inequality and the Weinberger inequality) provide a complete system of inequalities. Then we consider the case of convex plane domains for which we give new inequalities for the product $\\lambda_1 \\mu_1$λ 1​μ 1​. We plot the so-called Blaschke--Santal\\'o diagram and give some conjectures.\n\n### Keywords\n\nLaplace eigenvalues Dirichlet boundary Neumann boundary Faber-Krahn inequality Weinberger inequality Blaschke-Santaló diagram convex domains eigenvalue inequalities\n\n### Cite\n    \n    @article{arxiv.2501.02283,\n      title  = {The diagram $(\\lambda_1,\\mu_1)$},\n      author = {Ilias Ftouhi and Antoine Henrot},\n      journal= {arXiv preprint arXiv:2501.02283},\n      year   = {2025}\n    }"
